      en: "The Krahn-Bassa Hills form a critical watershed for central Liberia, feeding the St. Paul and Cavalla rivers. The hills are characterized by steep slopes and narrow ridges. Ecologically, they host a variety of primate species, including the Diana monkey. The region's economy is based on subsistence agriculture, with cassava and plantain as staple crops. Gold panning provides additional income. Deforestation for shifting cultivation has led to soil degradation.",
